**Read:** [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), full metals/alloys and selected graduate mechanism notes; [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC), the complete public problem/exam progression and a special-topic investigation; [Wood Handbook — Forest Products Laboratory, 2021](../sources/Wood-Handbook-FPL-2021.lingua#r_2SP2KMHCD78MQGZN69GKPGJ3WM), chapters 3–7 and 10–13; [Material families and mechanical response — Cambridge DoITPoMS](../sources/Material-Families-and-Mechanical-Response-DoITPoMS.lingua#r_79PNN694CQ82ENKZC6STQJ5KN9), plasticity, creep and wood packages. Read complete primary studies supporting the chosen metal and cellular material cases.

Connect processing and structure to deformation and failure in a metal and in wood or another documented cellular solid. Compare orientation, density/porosity, defects, temperature, moisture and rate without treating them as interchangeable fit parameters. Test a strengthening, creep or cellular scaling law against observations outside its fitted subset.

**Produce:** A quantitative account of two material states per family; a mechanism comparison supported by microscopy or equivalent evidence; one fatigue or creep history analysis; and uncertainty in the transfer from specimen to useful component. Explain why clear-wood properties or a small metal coupon do not alone establish product performance. Reconcile a contradictory observation and propose a discriminating follow-up.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Defend the material-family and mechanical-response account](Defend-the-material-family-and-mechanical-response-account.lingua#r_1SG5WSPXBJNEJ95BJ5ZB8NZ2D9).

